<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39919" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί-κτητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gained besides</i> or
				<i>in addition</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γῆ</span>
			<i>acquired</i> land, which was formerly under water, as the Delta
			of Egypt, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.5
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>; property <i>added to one's hereditary</i>
			<i>property</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				924a
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lycurg.
				48
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γυνή</span>
			<i>a foreign</i> wife (like <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπακτός</span>), or <i>newly acquired</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. φίλοι</span>
			<i>newly acquired</i> friends, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχαῖοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ages.</u>
				1.36
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. δόξα</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμφυτος ἐπιθυμία</span>, <i>acquired</i>
			perception, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				237d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐ.</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ φύσει ὄντα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>R.</u>
				618d
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύμφυτα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				721b30
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ αὐτοφυὲς τοῦ ἐ. αἱρετώτερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1365a29
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γίνεται . . ἐξ
			ἐπικτήτου</span>, of an <i>acquired</i> deformity, Paul.
				Aeg.<i><span class="en">
				6.29
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐ</span>. <i>property
				acquired after</i> a certain date, Edict.Aug. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Notiz.Arch.</u>
				4.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PGnom.</u>
				126
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Prisc.Lyd.
					21.15
				</span></i>
			.</div>
